.TH WEBSEARCHFS 4
.SH NAME
websearchfs, websearch \- answers from the web
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B websearchfs
[
.B -D
] [
.B -M
.I model
] [
.B -m
.I mtpt
] [
.B -s
.I srvname
] [
.B -u
.I url
]
.PP
.B websearch
.I query ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Websearchfs
serves one file,
.BR search ,
on
.I mtpt
.RB ( /mnt/websearch
by default), and posts itself as
.BI /srv/ srvname
if
.B -s
is given.
Open
.B search
for reading and writing, write a query, then read.
The first read sends the query to Anthropic's Messages API at
.I url
.RB ( https://api.anthropic.com ),
through
.IR webfs (4),
with the web search and web fetch tools, so the model can search the web
and fetch the pages that it needs or that the query names.
The read waits for the answer, then gives its text, a blank line, and the line
.B sources:
followed by each page the answer cites, once, as its URL, a tab and its title.
A failed search gives its error as the read's.
A write after an answer starts a new query.
.PP
The model is
.I model
.RB ( claude-sonnet-5-5 ).
The key is
.IR factotum (4)'s,
.BR "proto=pass service=anthropic" ,
read when the first query needs it.
A client of
.I websearchfs
never sees the key.
.PP
.I Websearch
writes its arguments as one query and prints the answer.
If
.B /mnt/websearch
has no
.BR search ,
it mounts
.BR /srv/websearch ,
or starts
.BR "websearchfs -s websearch" .
.PP
The
.B -D
option prints the 9P messages.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
% websearch when was Plan 9 first released
.EE
.PP
.I Sibyl
starts
.IR websearchfs ,
and
.B /lib/namespace.sibyl
mounts it in the name space of the model's commands, which have no
.IR factotum ,
so they can search but cannot read the key.
.SH FILES
.TF /lib/namespace.sibyl
.TP
.B /srv/websearch
.I websearchfs
as
.I sibyl
starts it
.TP
.B /lib/namespace.sibyl
mounts it on
.B /mnt/websearch
for
.IR sibyl 's
commands
.SH SOURCE
.B src/cmd/websearchfs
.br
.B rc/bin/websearch
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR factotum (4),
.IR webfs (4)
.SH BUGS
Each search is billed to the key's account, as are the tokens.
